{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791543,"nonce":"nzueiQJ0XEjt+CJUUxWfk/7A8H4=","title":"pointer_events_none on a div does not let hits through to its descendants' siblings underneath","message":"A div with pointer_events_none is skipped as a hit target, but its descendants (text, rows) are still hit-tested and capture the click. The click then bubbles up the parent chain and never reaches a sibling layer placed beneath the content. event_router.rs hit_test_node returns None for the node itself only when no child was hit.\n\nReproducer (blinc_layout 0.6.0): parent relative div with two children: a click layer (absolute, inset 0, on_click) first, and a content div with pointer_events_none holding a title text and a footer row. Click the centre of the parent: with only a text child the layer gets the click; once the content has a footer row with children, the click lands on the footer row or text and the layer never runs.\n\nExpected: pointer_events_none applies to the whole subtree (as CSS pointer-events does through inheritance), or there is a way to set it for a subtree.\n\nWorkaround in the caller: put the click layer above the content and the buttons after it as siblings.\n\nStand: waits for the Blinc team / fork; no change made here.","files":null}]}